TEXT 1104 704 Left 2 !.ic V(ncharge)=0
TEXT 936 16 Left 2 ;battery terminal path
TEXT 1104 664 Left 2 ;state of charge path
TEXT 1056 984 Left 2 !.tran 25000
TEXT 1056 848 Left 0 ;a 3000 mAh (3Ah) battery holds 3x3600 = 10800 Coulombs of total energy.\n \nBI divides sampled current by 1000, so time scale is expanded by 1000. \nThus, C = 10.8F to match scaling and represent 3Ah.
TEXT 1056 1040 Left 0 ;at 1.0 A rate, 2400 mAh takes 8640 seconds, or three hours.\n80% to 100% at a 0.2 A rate fills the remaining 600 mAh in 10800 seconds, so another three hours.\nTotal time thus takes approx 19440 seconds or 5.4 fours.
TEXT 1456 816 Left 0 ;This current source acts like an energy meter or a flow meter. It constantly measures the actual\nelectrical current flowing through the main charging wire (V_SENSE).\nBy feeing a matching current into the capacitor, it forces the capacitor to act as an integrator.\nIt charges up slowly over time to keep track of how full the battery\nis, giving us the value for "ncharge"
TEXT 1104 736 Left 2 !.options gfarad=0
TEXT 1104 760 Left 0 ;Disables LTspice's automatic parallel leakage resistor.
TEXT 1400 496 Left 0 ;This formula takes the battery's current fullness level (ncharge, which ranges from 0 to 1) and\nconverts it into a realistic electrical voltage.\n \nWhen the battery is completely empty (ncharge is 0), the\nformula evaluates to 3.6 + 0.6(0) = 3.6V, representing a discharged lithium-ion cell.\n \nAs the battery charges and ncjarge creeps toward 1, the voltage rises steadily.\n \nThe min function ensures that even if the calculation goes slightly over, the voltage is locked to a max ceiling of 4.2V so it never overcharges.
